        "original_id": "d913f653-284a-534a-ab30-d606193c8095",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Station Mall, Sault Ste. Marie, Ontario, Canada, Greater Sudbury, Thunder Bay\n- Companies: Walmart Canada, Walmart, Sears, Galaxy Cinemas, Woolco Canada, F. W. Woolworth Company\n- Products: New Sudbury Centre, Intercity Shopping Centre\n- Buildings: Sault Ste. Marie railway station\n\nFacts:\n- On March 17, 1994, Wal-Mart Canada Corp. was founded through Walmart’s purchase of the Woolco Canada chain from the F. W. Woolworth Company.\n- Wal-Mart Canada Corp. is the Canadian division of Walmart and is headquartered in Mississauga, Ontario.\n- Station Mall is in Sault Ste. Marie, Ontario, Canada.\n- Station Mall is the second largest shopping mall in Northern Ontario by area, behind New Sudbury Centre in Greater Sudbury.\n- Station Mall has fewer stores than Intercity Shopping Centre in Thunder Bay.\n- Station Mall’s major tenants include Sears, Walmart, and the 52,000-square-foot Galaxy Cinemas movie theatre complex.\n- The Sault Ste. Marie railway station building and passenger platform are located in the parking lot of Station Mall.",
